senses.gloss:
आ-√ ह्वे P. -ह्वयति (but also Pot. 1. sg. आ-हुवेम, AV. vii, 85, 1) Ā. -ह्वयते (but also 1. sg. आ॑-हुवे, RV.; aor. 3. pl. आ॑हूषत, RV. i, 14, 2, &c.; Inf. -हुव॑ध्यै, RV. vi, 60, 13, and -ह्वयितवै॑, ŚBr. ii, 5, 3, 18)
to call near, invoke invite, summon, cite, RV.; ŚBr.; TS.; MBh.; Mṛcch.; BhP.; Pañcat. &c.;
to provoke, challenge, emulate (in this sense only Ā. Pāṇ. i, 3, 31), RV.; ŚBr.; R.; Kathās. &c.;
to call to (especially in rites said of the Hotṛ, who addresses the Adhvaryu by the Ā-hāva or Ā-hvāna; see below), AitBr.; ĀśvŚr.; KātyŚr.; ŚāṅkhBr. & ŚāṅkhŚr.;
to proclaim, AitBr.; ŚBr.; KātyŚr.; ĀśvŚr. :
Caus. -ह्वाययति, to cause to call near, send for;
to cause to summon or challenge or invite, R.; Ragh.; Bhaṭṭ. :
Desid. -जुहूषति, to wish to call near, to be about to call near:
Intens. आ॑-जोहवीति, RV. vii, 56, 18, to call near zealously.
